{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>When there were no depths, I was brought forth</b> — its meaning is \"I made,\" and its sense is that of beginning and drawing near, from the language of: ואל שרה תחוללכם." "<b>When there were no springs, heavy with water</b> — its meaning is \"and when there were no springs heavy with water,\" and it is the notion of heaviness and abundance, and from it: התכבד כילק התכבדי כארבה."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:31.146552111Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}